    "markdown": "![ACL Logo](https://aclanthology.org/images/acl-logo.svg) ACL Anthology ⟨1⟩\n  * About⟨2⟩\n    * Announcements⟨3⟩\n    * Communication channels⟨4⟩\n    * Related work⟨5⟩\n    * Copyright⟨6⟩\n    * * * *\n    * Credits⟨7⟩\n    * Volunteer⟨8⟩\n    * Development⟨9⟩\n    * Feedback⟨10⟩\n  * Using⟨2⟩\n    * Citing papers⟨11⟩\n    * Links in the Anthology⟨12⟩\n    * Data access⟨13⟩\n    * * * *\n    * All FAQs⟨14⟩\n    * * * *\n    * ###### Details\n    * Anthology identifiers⟨15⟩\n    * Names⟨16⟩\n    * ORCID iDs⟨17⟩\n    * DOIs⟨18⟩\n    * Verified authors⟨19⟩\n  * Contributions⟨2⟩\n    * Submissions⟨20⟩\n    * Corrections⟨21⟩\n    * Author pages⟨22⟩\n    * Attachments⟨23⟩\n  * GitHub⟨24⟩\n\n\n##  Tapiwanashe Matangira ⟨22⟩\n* * *\n#### 2022\npdf ⟨25⟩bib ⟨26⟩abs⟨27⟩ ⟨28⟩\n**Quality at a Glance: An Audit of Web-Crawled Multilingual Datasets⟨29⟩**  \nJulia Kreutzer⟨30⟩ | Isaac Caswell⟨31⟩ | Lisa Wang⟨32⟩ | Ahsan Wahab⟨33⟩ | Daan van Esch⟨34⟩ | Nasanbayar Ulzii-Orshikh⟨35⟩ | Allahsera Tapo⟨36⟩ | Nishant Subramani⟨37⟩ | Artem Sokolov⟨38⟩ | Claytone Sikasote⟨39⟩ | Monang Setyawan⟨40⟩ | Supheakmungkol Sarin⟨41⟩ | Sokhar Samb⟨42⟩ | Benoît Sagot⟨43⟩ | Clara Rivera⟨44⟩ | Annette Rios⟨45⟩ | Isabel Papadimitriou⟨46⟩ | Salomey Osei⟨47⟩ | Pedro Ortiz Suarez⟨48⟩ | Iroro Orife⟨49⟩ | Kelechi Ogueji⟨50⟩ | Andre Niyongabo Rubungo⟨51⟩ | Toan Q. Nguyen⟨52⟩ | Mathias Müller⟨53⟩ | André Müller⟨54⟩ | Shamsuddeen Hassan Muhammad⟨55⟩ | Nanda Muhammad⟨56⟩ | Ayanda Mnyakeni⟨57⟩ | Jamshidbek Mirzakhalov⟨58⟩ | Tapiwanashe Matangira⟨59⟩ | Colin Leong⟨60⟩ | Nze Lawson⟨61⟩ | Sneha Kudugunta⟨62⟩ | Yacine Jernite⟨63⟩ | Mathias Jenny⟨64⟩ | Orhan Firat⟨65⟩ | Bonaventure F. P. Dossou⟨66⟩ | Sakhile Dlamini⟨67⟩ | Nisansa de Silva⟨68⟩ | Sakine Çabuk Ballı⟨69⟩ | Stella Biderman⟨70⟩ | Alessia Battisti⟨71⟩ | Ahmed Baruwa⟨72⟩ | Ankur Bapna⟨73⟩ | Pallavi Baljekar⟨74⟩ | Israel Abebe Azime⟨75⟩ | Ayodele Awokoya⟨76⟩ | Duygu Ataman⟨77⟩ | Orevaoghene Ahia⟨78⟩ | Oghenefego Ahia⟨79⟩ | Sweta Agrawal⟨80⟩ | Mofetoluwa Adeyemi⟨81⟩  \nTransactions of the Association for Computational Linguistics, Volume 10⟨82⟩\nWith the success of large-scale pre-training and multilingual modeling in Natural Language Processing (NLP), recent years have seen a proliferation of large, Web-mined text datasets covering hundreds of languages. We manually audit the quality of 205 language-specific corpora released with five major public datasets (CCAligned, ParaCrawl, WikiMatrix, OSCAR, mC4). Lower-resource corpora have systematic issues: At least 15 corpora have no usable text, and a significant fraction contains less than 50% sentences of acceptable quality. In addition, many are mislabeled or use nonstandard/ambiguous language codes. We demonstrate that these issues are easy to detect even for non-proficient speakers, and supplement the human audit with automatic analyses. Finally, we recommend techniques to evaluate and improve multilingual corpora and discuss potential risks that come with low-quality data releases.\nSearch⟨83⟩\n##### Co-authors\n  * Mofetoluwa Adeyemi⟨81⟩ 1\n  * Sweta Agrawal⟨80⟩ 1\n  * Oghenefego Ahia⟨79⟩ 1\n  * Orevaoghene Ahia⟨78⟩ 1\n  * Duygu Ataman⟨77⟩ 1\nshow all...\n  * Ayodele Awokoya⟨76⟩ 1\n  * Israel Abebe Azime⟨75⟩ 1\n  * Pallavi Baljekar⟨74⟩ 1\n  * Ankur Bapna⟨73⟩ 1\n  * Ahmed Baruwa⟨72⟩ 1\n  * Alessia Battisti⟨71⟩ 1\n  * Stella Biderman⟨70⟩ 1\n  * Isaac Caswell⟨31⟩ 1\n  * Nisansa De Silva⟨68⟩ 1\n  * Sakhile Dlamini⟨67⟩ 1\n  * Bonaventure F. P. Dossou⟨66⟩ 1\n  * Orhan Firat⟨65⟩ 1\n  * Mathias Jenny⟨64⟩ 1\n  * Yacine Jernite⟨63⟩ 1\n  * Julia Kreutzer⟨30⟩ 1\n  * Sneha Kudugunta⟨62⟩ 1\n  * Nze Lawson⟨61⟩ 1\n  * Colin Leong⟨60⟩ 1\n  * Jamshidbek Mirzakhalov⟨58⟩ 1\n  * Ayanda Mnyakeni⟨57⟩ 1\n  * Nanda Muhammad⟨56⟩ 1\n  * Shamsuddeen Hassan Muhammad⟨55⟩ 1\n  * André Müller⟨54⟩ 1\n  * Mathias Müller⟨53⟩ 1\n  * Toan Q. Nguyen⟨52⟩ 1\n  * Kelechi Ogueji⟨50⟩ 1\n  * Iroro Orife⟨49⟩ 1\n  * Pedro Ortiz Suarez⟨48⟩ 1\n  * Salomey Osei⟨47⟩ 1\n  * Isabel Papadimitriou⟨46⟩ 1\n  * Annette Rios Gonzales⟨45⟩ 1\n  * Clara Rivera⟨44⟩ 1\n  * Andre Niyongabo Rubungo⟨51⟩ 1\n  * Benoît Sagot⟨43⟩ 1\n  * Sokhar Samb⟨42⟩ 1\n  * Supheakmungkol Sarin⟨41⟩ 1\n  * Monang Setyawan⟨40⟩ 1\n  * Claytone Sikasote⟨39⟩ 1\n  * Artem Sokolov⟨38⟩ 1\n  * Nishant Subramani⟨37⟩ 1\n  * Allahsera Tapo⟨36⟩ 1\n  * Nasanbayar Ulzii-Orshikh⟨35⟩ 1\n  * Ahsan Wahab⟨33⟩ 1\n  * Lisa Wang⟨32⟩ 1\n  * Daan van Esch⟨34⟩ 1\n  * Sakine Çabuk Ballı⟨69⟩ 1\n\n\n##### Venues\n  * TACL⟨84⟩1\n\n\n Fix author⟨85⟩\n![Creative Commons License](https://i.creativecommons.org/l/by/4.0/88x31.png)⟨86⟩ ACL materials are Copyright © 1963–2026 ACL; other materials are copyrighted by their respective copyright holders. Materials prior to 2016 here are licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 3.0 International License⟨87⟩. Permission is granted to make copies for the purposes of teaching and research. Materials published in or after 2016 are licensed on a Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License⟨88⟩.\nThe ACL Anthology is managed and built by the ACL Anthology team⟨7⟩ of volunteers.\n_Site last built on 22 July 2026 at 14:46 UTC withcommit 280e4ed⟨89⟩._\n",
